<title>USA: RTZ' Kennecott, union begin talks in Utah.</title>
<headline>RTZ' Kennecott, union begin talks in Utah.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kennecott Utah Copper Corp and the United Steelworkers union began their first round of talks on Thursday since union workers went on strike, a union spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>The talks began at 0930 local/1530 GMT in an undisclosed location in Salt Lake City, said Carolyn Jensen, a union secretary.</p>
<p>Some 1,800 workers walked off their jobs at Kennecott on Wednesday. Their three-year labor contract expired on September 30.</p>
<p>The company is seeking a six-year contract. Kennecott operates a 310,000 short ton per year smelter which was operating at 75 percent of capacity prior to the strike, a company official said earlier this week.</p>
<p>Kennecott is a unit of London-based RTZ Corp Plc.</p>
